ShieldFont is a derivative work that does not use the Reserved Font
Names of any base font. Rendering is modified via injected OpenType
GSUB ligature rules; glyph outlines from each base font remain intact.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Shieldfont Optik — the shipped default variants (alpha, beta, gamma, max)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The default font variants this project ships (shieldfont-alpha / -beta /
-gamma / -max) are built on Optik, a commercial typeface by Playtype
<https://playtype.com>, and are distributed with Playtype's permission for
use as part of ShieldFont.

These font files contain Optik's letterforms and render them as any font
would. The permission covers using them to run ShieldFont's word-substitution
rendering — NOT use of Optik as a general-purpose typeface. You may not
extract, re-package, or use the underlying Optik typeface on its own; that
falls outside this permission and remains subject to Playtype's own license.
To use Optik as a typeface, obtain it from Playtype <https://playtype.com>.

The Optik-based variants are NOT covered by the SIL Open Font License or
LICENSE-FONTS. Those OFL terms apply only to variants you build from the OFL
base fonts (Inter, Syne Mono, Young Serif) via scripts/generate_font.py.

